<title>CHINA: Mongolia copper smelter says minor spill harmless.</title>
<headline>Mongolia copper smelter says minor spill harmless.</headline>
<dateline>BEIJING 1997-02-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Mongolian-U.S. mining joint venture Erdmin Co said on Thursday a minor spill at its recently opened copper solvent extraction plant in Mongolia had caused no casualties.</p>
<p>In a report on Wednesday, China's Xinhua news agency reported from Ulan Bator that the spill of sulphuric acid had killed five people.</p>
<p>&quot;In fact a minor release of a dilute solution last weeek caused no harm to human health and the environmental impact is considered to be minimal,&quot; Erdmin said in a statement faxed to Reuters in Beijing.</p>
</text>
